# Discord Bot Development

## Framework
- This project uses **Sapphire Framework** for Discord.js
- Follow Sapphire's patterns and conventions
- Use decorators provided by `@sapphire/decorators` (e.g., `@ApplyOptions`)

## Commands
- All commands should extend `ExtendedCommand` from `#lib/extensions/ExtendedCommand`
- Use `@ApplyOptions` to configure command options
- Commands should be in the `src/commands/` directory
- Register application commands in `registerApplicationCommands`
- Use `chatInputRun` for slash command handling
- Always use the `'cached'` interaction type: `ChatInputCommand.Interaction<'cached'>`
- Prefer early returns for error cases

## Preconditions
- Preconditions should extend `Precondition` from `@sapphire/framework`
- Use `@ApplyOptions` to configure position and other options
- Place in `src/preconditions/` directory
- Use `chatInputRun` for interaction-based preconditions
- Return `this.ok()` for success and `this.error()` for failure

## Listeners
- Listeners should be in `src/listeners/` directory
- Use appropriate event listener methods (e.g., `once`, `on`)
- Use decorators to register listeners automatically

## Interactions
- Always check for `'cached'` guild when accessing guild data
- Handle all interaction reply types appropriately
- Use `deferReply` for operations that take longer than 3 seconds

## Discord.js Patterns
- Use type-safe interaction guards (e.g., `interaction.inCachedGuild()`)
- Prefer modern Discord.js features and APIs
- Use Gateway Intents appropriately
- Configure Partials for needed data types

## Utilities
- Utility functions are in `src/lib/utils/`
- Export all utilities from `src/lib/utils/index.ts`
- Use path alias `#utils/*` to import utilities
- Organize utilities by category (discord, formatting, database, etc.)

## Configuration
- Use the Config class from `#lib/config/lib/Config` for configuration
- Configuration files are in `config/` directory
- Use Zod schemas for configuration validation
- Register configuration in `src/lib/config/register.ts`
